From: libkrun boot optimization
Subject: [PATCH] virtio_blk: skip partition scan at probe time

For microVM use cases where the block device is always a single
unpartitioned filesystem, the partition scan in device_add_disk()
reads the partition table via virtio I/O, causing ~8ms of probe
latency. Set GENHD_FL_NO_PART so disk_scan_partitions() returns
immediately without any I/O.

The disk is accessible as /dev/vda (whole device, no /dev/vdaN).
Format the image as raw ext4 without a partition table.

--- a/drivers/block/virtio_blk.c
+++ b/drivers/block/virtio_blk.c
@@ -1514,6 +1514,9 @@ static int virtblk_probe(struct virtio_device *vdev)
 	vblk->disk->minors = 1 << PART_BITS;
 	vblk->disk->private_data = vblk;
 	vblk->disk->fops = &virtblk_fops;
+	/* Skip partition table scan: microVM block devices are always
+	 * single unpartitioned filesystems; avoids I/O at probe time. */
+	vblk->disk->flags |= GENHD_FL_NO_PART;
 	vblk->index = index;

 	/* If disk is read-only in the host, the guest should obey */
